{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RspptrKfmdyGkAhcqGx7tN","type":"tool_result","content":"        \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.combined_score\",\n        \"final.metric.control_permuted_score\",\n        \"final.metric.combined_minus_control_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_label_low_budget\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_label_high_budget\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        5,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 7.5,\n      \"figure_id\": \"error_accounting\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"composite\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 8.5,\n        \"legend\": 8,\n        \"ticks\": 8,\n        \"title\": 8.5\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 36,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/error_accounting.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/error_accounting.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        1,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.combined_score\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic\",\n        \"final.metric.control_permuted_score\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"selected_prompt_family\": \"paper_standalone\",\n  \"recommended_title\": \"When Is One Kernel SHAP Run Enough? Predicting Top-3 Attribution Reproducibility from a Single Budgeted Run\",\n  \"central_question\": \"For a trained tabular classifier explained by a budget-limited Kernel SHAP run, how often does the single run's top-3 feature set agree with independent reruns, and can that agreement be predicted from the single run's own coalition data better than trivial and split-half baselines?\",\n  \"central_thesis\": \"Single-run Kernel SHAP top-3 reproducibility is conditional rather than uniformly high (mean agreement 0.807 at a 4d coalition budget vs 0.932 at 16d on the held-out evaluation datasets), and a diagnostic computed only from the assessed run predicts it with lower squared error than always-reliable, constant-0.5 and split-half-gap baselines, but only modestly above a pairing-permuted control, so most of its skill is budget-level calibration and per-instance resolution is limited (Spearman 0.58).\",\n  \"narrative_rationale\": \"The final evaluation completed with outcome qualified (final.qualification.outcome), with positive lower confidence bounds against all three evaluator baselines and against the permuted-pairing control, so a measured-results paper is supportable. The artifacts do not support the original brief's broad empirical study (no per-dataset/per-model breakdown, no background-size or retraining-noise experiments, no deep tabular models, no ablation_studies). The strongest coherent story is therefore a bounded one: define single-run reproducibility operationally (top-3 Jaccard against 8 reruns), show it depends on coalition budget, and evaluate a single-run self-diagnostic against honest baselines and a control, stating loudly that the gain over the control is small. This is thesis-first and avoids the three-attempt search chronology; search is demoted to a short supplementary robustness note because there are no ablations that attribute the gain to components.\",\n  \"prior_paper_story_status\": \"rejected\",\n  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"Not edit mode: no previous_paper directory or edit-context files exist. Fresh framing; no prior thesis to preserve.\",\n  \"staged_input_impact\": [\n    \"No staged prior manuscript or new-program inputs; framing derives only from paper_data.json (final_evaluation, result.* search sources), task/task_contract.json, and evaluator source for the label/baseline definitions.\",\n    \"paper_data.json has no downstream_study key, so no downstream-study comparison is planned.\"\n  ],\n  \"method_groups\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Single-run reproducibility label (measurement protocol)\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Defines the object being predicted: for each explained instance, mean top-3 Jaccard agreement between the assessed Kernel SHAP run and 8 independent reruns, at coalition budgets 4d and 16d, background 32 rows, three model families (logistic regression, random forest, sklearn MLP). Needed to state the conditional-reliability claim (final.metric.mean_label_low_budget / mean_label_high_budget).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Single-run self-diagnostic (frozen selected configuration)\",\n      \"role\": \"proposed\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"The studied method: from one run's coalition masks, weights and values it simulates reruns via a delete-one-group jackknife (4 partitions, antithetic common-random-number draws), shrinks toward a budget-dependent prior and adds a small margin gate, outputting r_hat in [0,1]. Constants are hand-set and untuned; say so.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Evaluator-owned reference baselines\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Always-reliable (r=1), constant 0.5, and a split-half-gap heuristic computed from the same single run. Grounded via final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable, skill_vs_constant_half, skill_vs_gap_heuristic and their CI lows. The original search-time baseline program has no grounded score in paper_data, so that comparison is omitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Label-permuted pairing control\",\n      \"role\": \"ablation\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Shuffles which r_hat is paired with which instance label (20 deterministic derangements) to separate budget/cell-level calibration from instance-specific information. Score 0.9701 vs diagnostic 0.9838 (final.metric.control_permuted_score, combined_minus_control_ci_low). The key calibration guard of the paper.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Search-plane model variants (three configurations)\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Supplement-only: three scored configurations on search datasets (result.improvement_001..003) show the selection and that differences are small; no component ablations exist, so no mechanistic attribution is claimed. All 3 attempts were scored; there are no unscored attempts.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_focus\": [\n    \"Conditional reliability: final mean label 0.8065 at 4d vs 0.9315 at 16d budget (final.metric.mean_label_low_budget, mean_label_high_budget); single-run top-3 set reproducibility is not uniformly high, and the low-budget regime is where one run is least trustworthy. Do not break this down by dataset or model family; no grounded breakdown exists.\",\n    \"Diagnostic accuracy on final data: combined score 0.9838 (= 1 - mean squared error, so MSE about 0.0162; derived arithmetic, label it derived) with seed-level scores 0.9850 and 0.9826 (final.evidence.episodes, seeds 9001/9002).\",\n    \"Skill over baselines with one-sided 2.5th-percentile bootstrap lower bounds: vs always-reliable +0.0353 (low 0.0171), vs constant 0.5 +0.1543 (low 0.1245), vs split-half gap heuristic +0.0122 (low 0.0081). Only lower bounds are available; do not fabricate upper bounds or symmetric intervals.\",\n    \"Honest control: permuted-pairing score 0.9701; diagnostic minus control = 0.0137 (derived), lower bound 0.0101. Interpret as real but small instance-specific information on top of budget-level calibration; Spearman between r_hat and label 0.581 indicates moderate ranking ability.\",\n    \"Scale of the gain in plain terms: root-mean-squared error about 0.127 for the diagnostic vs about 0.227 for always-reliable (both derived from grounded metrics; label as derived).\",\n    \"Selection is reported separately from the final evaluation: search scores 0.9760, 0.9837, 0.9854 for three scored configurations on the search datasets; the frozen selected configuration is the 0.9854 one. Per-attempt two-seed ranges overlap, so the ordering is not claimed significant.\",\n    \"Final outcome is qualified (final.qualification.outcome); no failed-qualification disclosure needed, but qualification does not turn these bounded metrics into general validity claims.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_plan\": [\n    \"Fig. 1 (overview, early): the measurement protocol and claim structure at a glance: trained model + instance -> one assessed Kernel SHAP run at budget 4d or 16d -> diagnostic outputs r_hat; evaluator reruns 8 times -> top-3 Jaccard label; scoring against always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap, permuted control.\",\n    \"Fig. 2 (main evidence, two panels): (a) skill (MSE reduction) over always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap heuristic, and over permuted control, with one-sided bootstrap lower-bound markers; (b) mean single-run top-3 agreement at 4d vs 16d budget.\",\n    \"Table 1 (native LaTeX): final metrics with lower bounds, seed-level scores and the derived MSE/RMSE column marked as derived.\",\n    \"Supplement Fig./Table: search-plane scores of the three configurations with per-seed values (supporting only).\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_specs\": [\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"protocol_overview\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Give glance value for the setting: what a single run is, what the label measures (top-3 Jaccard vs 8 reruns), what the diagnostic sees, and what it is scored against.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"group_by\": \"protocol_stage\",\n      \"metric\": \"none (conceptual)\",\n      \"split_by\": \"none\",\n      \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n      \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"layout_rationale\": \"ICLR style is single-column (text width about 5.5 in); a left-to-right pipeline with 4-5 boxes and short labels needs the full text width to keep text at or above about 7 pt. Place on page 1 or 2.\",\n      \"allow_progression\": false,\n      \"max_panels\": 1,\n      \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n      \"max_series_per_panel\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"main_comparison\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Show (a) diagnostic skill over each baseline and over the permuted control with lower-bound markers and (b) budget-conditional single-run agreement.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"two_panel_bar\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"group_by\": \"comparator\",\ngenerate-concept-figure\nmemory-log\nretrieve-references\nscientific-evidence\nvalidate-paper\nwrite-paper-standalone\nanalysis:\nbuild_figures.py\nderive_metrics.py\nderived_metrics.json\nderived_metrics.json.prov.json\n\nsource_evidence:\nevaluator_final.py\nfinal_manifest.json\nfinal_resources_manifest.json\nsearch_eval_evidence_selected.json\nsearch_resources_manifest.json\nsearchplane_config_A_program.py\nsearchplane_config_B_program.py\nselected_config_NOTES.md\nselected_config_program.py\ntask_contract.json","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ff39c7c-7e6c-4623-8675-53e5f2cce2d4","uuid":"a0b525c9-3619-4074-86da-dd1258df95ea","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:47:05.046Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"        \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.combined_score\",\n        \"final.metric.control_permuted_score\",\n        \"final.metric.combined_minus_control_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_label_low_budget\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_label_high_budget\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        5,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 7.5,\n      \"figure_id\": \"error_accounting\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"composite\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 8.5,\n        \"legend\": 8,\n        \"ticks\": 8,\n        \"title\": 8.5\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 36,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/error_accounting.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/error_accounting.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        1,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.combined_score\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_constant_half\",\n        \"final.metric.skill_vs_gap_heuristic\",\n        \"final.metric.control_permuted_score\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"selected_prompt_family\": \"paper_standalone\",\n  \"recommended_title\": \"When Is One Kernel SHAP Run Enough? Predicting Top-3 Attribution Reproducibility from a Single Budgeted Run\",\n  \"central_question\": \"For a trained tabular classifier explained by a budget-limited Kernel SHAP run, how often does the single run's top-3 feature set agree with independent reruns, and can that agreement be predicted from the single run's own coalition data better than trivial and split-half baselines?\",\n  \"central_thesis\": \"Single-run Kernel SHAP top-3 reproducibility is conditional rather than uniformly high (mean agreement 0.807 at a 4d coalition budget vs 0.932 at 16d on the held-out evaluation datasets), and a diagnostic computed only from the assessed run predicts it with lower squared error than always-reliable, constant-0.5 and split-half-gap baselines, but only modestly above a pairing-permuted control, so most of its skill is budget-level calibration and per-instance resolution is limited (Spearman 0.58).\",\n  \"narrative_rationale\": \"The final evaluation completed with outcome qualified (final.qualification.outcome), with positive lower confidence bounds against all three evaluator baselines and against the permuted-pairing control, so a measured-results paper is supportable. The artifacts do not support the original brief's broad empirical study (no per-dataset/per-model breakdown, no background-size or retraining-noise experiments, no deep tabular models, no ablation_studies). The strongest coherent story is therefore a bounded one: define single-run reproducibility operationally (top-3 Jaccard against 8 reruns), show it depends on coalition budget, and evaluate a single-run self-diagnostic against honest baselines and a control, stating loudly that the gain over the control is small. This is thesis-first and avoids the three-attempt search chronology; search is demoted to a short supplementary robustness note because there are no ablations that attribute the gain to components.\",\n  \"prior_paper_story_status\": \"rejected\",\n  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"Not edit mode: no previous_paper directory or edit-context files exist. Fresh framing; no prior thesis to preserve.\",\n  \"staged_input_impact\": [\n    \"No staged prior manuscript or new-program inputs; framing derives only from paper_data.json (final_evaluation, result.* search sources), task/task_contract.json, and evaluator source for the label/baseline definitions.\",\n    \"paper_data.json has no downstream_study key, so no downstream-study comparison is planned.\"\n  ],\n  \"method_groups\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Single-run reproducibility label (measurement protocol)\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Defines the object being predicted: for each explained instance, mean top-3 Jaccard agreement between the assessed Kernel SHAP run and 8 independent reruns, at coalition budgets 4d and 16d, background 32 rows, three model families (logistic regression, random forest, sklearn MLP). Needed to state the conditional-reliability claim (final.metric.mean_label_low_budget / mean_label_high_budget).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Single-run self-diagnostic (frozen selected configuration)\",\n      \"role\": \"proposed\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"The studied method: from one run's coalition masks, weights and values it simulates reruns via a delete-one-group jackknife (4 partitions, antithetic common-random-number draws), shrinks toward a budget-dependent prior and adds a small margin gate, outputting r_hat in [0,1]. Constants are hand-set and untuned; say so.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Evaluator-owned reference baselines\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Always-reliable (r=1), constant 0.5, and a split-half-gap heuristic computed from the same single run. Grounded via final.metric.skill_vs_always_reliable, skill_vs_constant_half, skill_vs_gap_heuristic and their CI lows. The original search-time baseline program has no grounded score in paper_data, so that comparison is omitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Label-permuted pairing control\",\n      \"role\": \"ablation\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Shuffles which r_hat is paired with which instance label (20 deterministic derangements) to separate budget/cell-level calibration from instance-specific information. Score 0.9701 vs diagnostic 0.9838 (final.metric.control_permuted_score, combined_minus_control_ci_low). The key calibration guard of the paper.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Search-plane model variants (three configurations)\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Supplement-only: three scored configurations on search datasets (result.improvement_001..003) show the selection and that differences are small; no component ablations exist, so no mechanistic attribution is claimed. All 3 attempts were scored; there are no unscored attempts.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_focus\": [\n    \"Conditional reliability: final mean label 0.8065 at 4d vs 0.9315 at 16d budget (final.metric.mean_label_low_budget, mean_label_high_budget); single-run top-3 set reproducibility is not uniformly high, and the low-budget regime is where one run is least trustworthy. Do not break this down by dataset or model family; no grounded breakdown exists.\",\n    \"Diagnostic accuracy on final data: combined score 0.9838 (= 1 - mean squared error, so MSE about 0.0162; derived arithmetic, label it derived) with seed-level scores 0.9850 and 0.9826 (final.evidence.episodes, seeds 9001/9002).\",\n    \"Skill over baselines with one-sided 2.5th-percentile bootstrap lower bounds: vs always-reliable +0.0353 (low 0.0171), vs constant 0.5 +0.1543 (low 0.1245), vs split-half gap heuristic +0.0122 (low 0.0081). Only lower bounds are available; do not fabricate upper bounds or symmetric intervals.\",\n    \"Honest control: permuted-pairing score 0.9701; diagnostic minus control = 0.0137 (derived), lower bound 0.0101. Interpret as real but small instance-specific information on top of budget-level calibration; Spearman between r_hat and label 0.581 indicates moderate ranking ability.\",\n    \"Scale of the gain in plain terms: root-mean-squared error about 0.127 for the diagnostic vs about 0.227 for always-reliable (both derived from grounded metrics; label as derived).\",\n    \"Selection is reported separately from the final evaluation: search scores 0.9760, 0.9837, 0.9854 for three scored configurations on the search datasets; the frozen selected configuration is the 0.9854 one. Per-attempt two-seed ranges overlap, so the ordering is not claimed significant.\",\n    \"Final outcome is qualified (final.qualification.outcome); no failed-qualification disclosure needed, but qualification does not turn these bounded metrics into general validity claims.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_plan\": [\n    \"Fig. 1 (overview, early): the measurement protocol and claim structure at a glance: trained model + instance -> one assessed Kernel SHAP run at budget 4d or 16d -> diagnostic outputs r_hat; evaluator reruns 8 times -> top-3 Jaccard label; scoring against always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap, permuted control.\",\n    \"Fig. 2 (main evidence, two panels): (a) skill (MSE reduction) over always-reliable, constant 0.5, split-half gap heuristic, and over permuted control, with one-sided bootstrap lower-bound markers; (b) mean single-run top-3 agreement at 4d vs 16d budget.\",\n    \"Table 1 (native LaTeX): final metrics with lower bounds, seed-level scores and the derived MSE/RMSE column marked as derived.\",\n    \"Supplement Fig./Table: search-plane scores of the three configurations with per-seed values (supporting only).\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_specs\": [\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"protocol_overview\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Give glance value for the setting: what a single run is, what the label measures (top-3 Jaccard vs 8 reruns), what the diagnostic sees, and what it is scored against.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"group_by\": \"protocol_stage\",\n      \"metric\": \"none (conceptual)\",\n      \"split_by\": \"none\",\n      \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n      \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"layout_rationale\": \"ICLR style is single-column (text width about 5.5 in); a left-to-right pipeline with 4-5 boxes and short labels needs the full text width to keep text at or above about 7 pt. Place on page 1 or 2.\",\n      \"allow_progression\": false,\n      \"max_panels\": 1,\n      \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n    