{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6f2Hkov5RkKnQ9afW9WW9","type":"tool_result","content":"254\t\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\n255\t\\toprule\n256\tPredictor & MSE & RMSE & MSE reduction by diagnostic \\\\\n257\t\\midrule\n258\tDiagnostic & 0.0162 & 0.127 & -- \\\\\n259\tSplit-half gap & 0.0284 & 0.169 & 42.9\\% \\\\\n260\tPermuted control & 0.0299 & 0.173 & 45.9\\% \\\\\n261\tAlways reliable & 0.0515 & 0.227 & 68.5\\% \\\\\n262\tConstant 0.5 & 0.1705 & 0.413 & 90.5\\% \\\\\n263\t\\bottomrule\n264\t\\end{tabular}\n265\t\\end{table}\n266\tThe bounds on non-identical top-3 sets follow from the Jaccard values $\\{0,0.2,0.5,1\\}$ for overlaps $\\{0,1,2,3\\}$: a pair with non-identical sets loses between 0.5 and 1 of the maximal agreement, so a mean loss $D$ implies a non-identical share $q$ with $D\\le q\\le 2D$. The gain over always-reliable splits into $0.0216$ retained under permutation (the always-reliable MSE minus the control MSE) and $0.0137$ instance-specific.\n267\t\n268\t\\subsection{Selected configuration constants}\n269\t\\begin{table}[h]\n270\t\\centering\n271\t\\caption{Constants of the frozen self-diagnostic. None was fitted to instance labels; the budget-prior values 0.84 and 0.96 are aggregate label means by budget taken from earlier search-plane evaluations.}\n272\t\\label{tab:consts}\n273\t\\small\n274\t\\begin{tabular}{lll}\n275\t\\toprule\n276\tConstant & Value & Role \\\\\n277\t\\midrule\n278\tFolds / partitions & 8 / 4 & delete-one-group jackknife, averaged \\\\\n279\tDraws & 1000 (500 antithetic) & common random numbers per episode \\\\\n280\tSimulator weights ($s_{d,1}$, $s_{d,0.7}$, $s_{f,1}$) & 0.5, 0.2, 0.3 & convex combination \\\\\n281\tPrior at $B=4d$ / $16d$ & 0.84 / 0.96 & from earlier aggregate label means \\\\\n282\tPrior weight & 0.4 & shrinkage toward prior \\\\\n283\tMargin term & 0.02, scale 3 & soft gate, $\\tanh(z_{\\mathrm m}/3)$ \\\\\n284\tOutput clip & $[0.02,1]$ & numerical safety \\\\\n285\t\\bottomrule\n286\t\\end{tabular}\n287\t\\end{table}\n288\tThe notes accompanying the configuration state that it was written without executing any code, so no local calibration or cross-validation exists for it and none is claimed. Its search-plane score was obtained only from the evaluator.\n289\t\n290\t\\subsection{Search-plane scores of the three configurations}\n291\tThree configurations were scored on the search plane; all three completed successfully and none was unscored. The search label is evaluator-defined, so it is the same quantity as in the final evaluation, but the datasets differ, and these scores are development proxies. Table~\\ref{tab:search} lists them. Configuration~A is a single-partition jackknife with full covariance and a $\\sqrt2$ inflation of the simulated spread and 400 draws. Configuration~B replaces this with common-random-number draws, diagonal and full-covariance simulators and a fixed convex combination. Configuration~C, the selection, adds the partition ensemble, the budget prior and the margin term (\\texttt{searchplane\\_config\\_A\\_program.py}, \\texttt{searchplane\\_config\\_B\\_program.py}, \\texttt{selected\\_config\\_program.py}). Because several changes were made at once and no ablation was run, no change is credited with a score difference. The per-seed ranges of B and C overlap, and A is lower than both on each of the two seeds.\n292\t\\begin{table}[h]\n293\t\\centering\n294\t\\caption{Search-plane scores ($1-\\text{MSE}$) by seed. Search seeds are 101 and 102.}\n295\t\\label{tab:search}\n296\t\\small\n297\t\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\n298\t\\toprule\n299\tConfiguration & Seed 101 & Seed 102 & Mean \\\\\n300\t\\midrule\n301\tA (inflated full-covariance jackknife) & 0.9740 & 0.9779 & 0.9760 \\\\\n302\tB (common-random-number combination) & 0.9824 & 0.9849 & 0.9837 \\\\\n303\tC (selected: B + partitions, prior, margin) & 0.9840 & 0.9869 & 0.9854 \\\\\n304\t\\bottomrule\n305\t\\end{tabular}\n306\t\\end{table}\n307\t% @evidence[[paper_data.json#all_programs]]\n308\t\n309\t\\subsection{Reproducibility statement}\n310\tThe evaluator source, task contract, manifests and the source of the selected configuration are in \\texttt{source\\_evidence/}. The scripts \\texttt{analysis/derive\\_metrics.py} and \\texttt{analysis/build\\_figures.py} regenerate Table~\\ref{tab:derived} and Figures~\\ref{fig:main} and~\\ref{fig:accounting} from \\texttt{paper\\_data.json}. Figure~\\ref{fig:overview} is a schematic with no quantitative content. We did not re-run the sealed evaluation, and per-cell labels and per-instance outputs from it are not part of the retained evidence.\n311\t\n312\t\\subsection{LLM usage}\n313\tLarge language models were used in this work in two roles. First, an LLM-based research agent proposed and implemented the candidate diagnostics, and the sealed evaluator, not the agent, scored them. Second, an LLM drafted this manuscript from the recorded evaluator outputs and source files, and generated the analysis and figure scripts. Every number in the paper was checked against the recorded evaluator outputs or computed from them by the included scripts. No LLM output was used as a source of experimental results. References were retrieved from bibliographic databases; our descriptions of cited works rely on their public titles and on the model's prior knowledge, and the papers were not re-read in full while writing.\n314\t\n315\t\\end{document}\n316\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ff39c7c-7e6c-4623-8675-53e5f2cce2d4","uuid":"7b44beeb-f031-4242-bef7-623f156795c3","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:47:16.209Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/paper/paper.tex","content":"\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\n\\toprule\nPredictor & MSE & RMSE & MSE reduction by diagnostic \\\\\n\\midrule\nDiagnostic & 0.0162 & 0.127 & -- \\\\\nSplit-half gap & 0.0284 & 0.169 & 42.9\\% \\\\\nPermuted control & 0.0299 & 0.173 & 45.9\\% \\\\\nAlways reliable & 0.0515 & 0.227 & 68.5\\% \\\\\nConstant 0.5 & 0.1705 & 0.413 & 90.5\\% \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\nThe bounds on non-identical top-3 sets follow from the Jaccard values $\\{0,0.2,0.5,1\\}$ for overlaps $\\{0,1,2,3\\}$: a pair with non-identical sets loses between 0.5 and 1 of the maximal agreement, so a mean loss $D$ implies a non-identical share $q$ with $D\\le q\\le 2D$. The gain over always-reliable splits into $0.0216$ retained under permutation (the always-reliable MSE minus the control MSE) and $0.0137$ instance-specific.\n\n\\subsection{Selected configuration constants}\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Constants of the frozen self-diagnostic. None was fitted to instance labels; the budget-prior values 0.84 and 0.96 are aggregate label means by budget taken from earlier search-plane evaluations.}\n\\label{tab:consts}\n\\small\n\\begin{tabular}{lll}\n\\toprule\nConstant & Value & Role \\\\\n\\midrule\nFolds / partitions & 8 / 4 & delete-one-group jackknife, averaged \\\\\nDraws & 1000 (500 antithetic) & common random numbers per episode \\\\\nSimulator weights ($s_{d,1}$, $s_{d,0.7}$, $s_{f,1}$) & 0.5, 0.2, 0.3 & convex combination \\\\\nPrior at $B=4d$ / $16d$ & 0.84 / 0.96 & from earlier aggregate label means \\\\\nPrior weight & 0.4 & shrinkage toward prior \\\\\nMargin term & 0.02, scale 3 & soft gate, $\\tanh(z_{\\mathrm m}/3)$ \\\\\nOutput clip & $[0.02,1]$ & numerical safety \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\nThe notes accompanying the configuration state that it was written without executing any code, so no local calibration or cross-validation exists for it and none is claimed. Its search-plane score was obtained only from the evaluator.\n\n\\subsection{Search-plane scores of the three configurations}\nThree configurations were scored on the search plane; all three completed successfully and none was unscored. The search label is evaluator-defined, so it is the same quantity as in the final evaluation, but the datasets differ, and these scores are development proxies. Table~\\ref{tab:search} lists them. Configuration~A is a single-partition jackknife with full covariance and a $\\sqrt2$ inflation of the simulated spread and 400 draws. Configuration~B replaces this with common-random-number draws, diagonal and full-covariance simulators and a fixed convex combination. Configuration~C, the selection, adds the partition ensemble, the budget prior and the margin term (\\texttt{searchplane\\_config\\_A\\_program.py}, \\texttt{searchplane\\_config\\_B\\_program.py}, \\texttt{selected\\_config\\_program.py}). Because several changes were made at once and no ablation was run, no change is credited with a score difference. The per-seed ranges of B and C overlap, and A is lower than both on each of the two seeds.\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Search-plane scores ($1-\\text{MSE}$) by seed. Search seeds are 101 and 102.}\n\\label{tab:search}\n\\small\n\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\n\\toprule\nConfiguration & Seed 101 & Seed 102 & Mean \\\\\n\\midrule\nA (inflated full-covariance jackknife) & 0.9740 & 0.9779 & 0.9760 \\\\\nB (common-random-number combination) & 0.9824 & 0.9849 & 0.9837 \\\\\nC (selected: B + partitions, prior, margin) & 0.9840 & 0.9869 & 0.9854 \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#all_programs]]\n\n\\subsection{Reproducibility statement}\nThe evaluator source, task contract, manifests and the source of the selected configuration are in \\texttt{source\\_evidence/}. The scripts \\texttt{analysis/derive\\_metrics.py} and \\texttt{analysis/build\\_figures.py} regenerate Table~\\ref{tab:derived} and Figures~\\ref{fig:main} and~\\ref{fig:accounting} from \\texttt{paper\\_data.json}. Figure~\\ref{fig:overview} is a schematic with no quantitative content. We did not re-run the sealed evaluation, and per-cell labels and per-instance outputs from it are not part of the retained evidence.\n\n\\subsection{LLM usage}\nLarge language models were used in this work in two roles. First, an LLM-based research agent proposed and implemented the candidate diagnostics, and the sealed evaluator, not the agent, scored them. Second, an LLM drafted this manuscript from the recorded evaluator outputs and source files, and generated the analysis and figure scripts. Every number in the paper was checked against the recorded evaluator outputs or computed from them by the included scripts. No LLM output was used as a source of experimental results. References were retrieved from bibliographic databases; our descriptions of cited works rely on their public titles and on the model's prior knowledge, and the papers were not re-read in full while writing.\n\n\\end{document}\n","numLines":63,"startLine":254,"totalLines":316}}}
