{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvrMUKNeYadwbHfRXCtb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed both audit findings and the figure-manifest error. `paper.tex` compiles (13 pages), but two of the standard checks and the global-memory log could not run here.\n\n**Audit finding on the budget prior**\n- The abstract now says the 0.84/0.96 prior values are hand-set. It also says the configuration's notes describe them as aggregate label means from earlier evaluation metrics, but those means aren't kept in the evidence, so their origin can't be checked.\n- The Method provenance paragraph, the Table 4 caption and row, and the statistical-limits paragraph got the same correction. The unqualified \"search-plane\" wording is gone. The grounding claim for the prior no longer cites the final-evaluation label means (0.8065 and 0.9315).\n\n**Audit finding on protocol and constant claims**\n- The Method protocol text and the Table 4 caption now say these facts are read from `source_evidence/evaluator_final.py`, `task_contract.json` and `selected_config_program.py`, with line ranges. They state that these facts do not come from the sealed metrics.\n- In `claims_grounding.json` the protocol-fact and diagnostic-constant claims now name those files and lines, and I added a separate claim for the German Credit hash-split disjointness. Their source ids are `final.evidence.episodes` and `result.improvement_003`, used only as provenance pointers because `paper_data.json` has no source that carries these constants. The source-file claims therefore still can't be fully resolved through the registry.\n\n**Figure manifest**\n- I changed `main_comparison`'s `figure_type` from `two_panel_bar` to `composite`, so the manifest now has the allowed values and lists all three figures. I did not run the schema validator (see below).\n\n**Checks**\n- `validate_tex_refs.py` passes (30 citation keys), and `validate_claims.py` passes (30 grounded claims).\n- The scientific-evidence verifier reports 60 references with 0 dangling.\n- `pdflatex` and `bibtex` compile with no undefined references.\n\n**Not run or not updated**\n- `validate_figures.py` failed because the `src` package isn't importable here, and `compile_latex.sh` needs `pdftotext`, which isn't installed. The figure-manifest fix and the rendered-SI check are therefore unconfirmed until the orchestrator re-validates.\n- `global_memory/` is a dangling symlink to `../investigation`, so I logged the repair only in `./memory.md`.\n\nThe paper's qualified outcome and its limitations (small gain over the permuted control, no ablations, hand-set constants) are unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":94414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"output_tokens":689,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ff39c7c-7e6c-4623-8675-53e5f2cce2d4","uuid":"a733afcb-2cfd-4cab-8a41-01b58c455100","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:48:41.103Z","request_id":"req_011CgvrMSUEk2ay2J6nwTSRj"}
